<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Standard deviation of grouped data</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(w=10)"]]The table shows the time, \(t\) minutes, that \({@n@}\) learners spent on homework one evening.[[else]]The table shows the distance, \(d\) km, ridden in a day by \({@n@}\) boda boda riders in Kisumu.[[/if]]</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(w=10)"]]Time (minutes)[[else]]Distance (km)[[/if]]</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[1]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[1]+w@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[2]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[2]+w@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[3]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[3]+w@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[4]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[4]+w@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[5]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[5]+w@}\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(k=6)"]]\({@lo[6]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[6]+w@}\)[[/if]]</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (\(f\))</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(k=6)"]]{@f[6]@}[[/if]]</td></tr></table><p>Use the class midpoints, \(x\).</p><p>(a) Find \(\Sigma fx\).</p><div>\(\Sigma fx =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find \(\Sigma fx^2\).</p><div>\(\Sigma fx^2 =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Estimate the mean, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div>\(\bar{x} =\) [[input:ans3]] [[if test="is(w=10)"]]minutes[[else]]km[[/if]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Estimate the standard deviation, correct to 2 decimal places. Do not round until the final answer.</p><div>\(\sigma =\) [[input:ans4]] [[if test="is(w=10)"]]minutes[[else]]km[[/if]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Grouped data do not give the exact values, so we place every value at the midpoint of its class. The mean and standard deviation found this way are estimates.</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Class</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (\(f\))</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Midpoint (\(x\))</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(fx\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(fx^2\)</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[1]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[1]+w@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@mid[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx[1])@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx2[1])@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[2]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[2]+w@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@mid[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx[2])@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx2[2])@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[3]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[3]+w@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@mid[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx[3])@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx2[3])@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[4]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[4]+w@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@mid[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx[4])@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx2[4])@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[5]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[5]+w@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@mid[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx[5])@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx2[5])@}\)</td></tr>[[if test="is(k=6)"]]<tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@lo[6]@} \le {@vl@} \lt {@lo[6]+w@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@mid[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx[6])@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(fx2[6])@}\)</td></tr>[[/if]]<tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Total</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@n@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;"></td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(Sfx)@}\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@grpm(Sfx2)@}\)</td></tr></table><p>(a) \(\Sigma fx = {@grpm(Sfx)@}\). (b) \(\Sigma fx^2 = {@grpm(Sfx2)@}\).</p><p>(c) \[\bar{x} = \frac{\Sigma fx}{\Sigma f} = \frac{ {@grpm(Sfx)@} }{ {@n@} } \approx {@mnd@}\]</p><p>(d) The variance is the mean of the squares minus the square of the mean. Keep \(\bar{x}\) unrounded: \[\sigma^2 = \frac{\Sigma fx^2}{\Sigma f} - \bar{x}^2 = \frac{ {@grpm(Sfx2)@} }{ {@n@} } - {@mn3d@}^2 \approx {@vrd@}\]so \(\sigma = \sqrt{\sigma^2} \approx {@sdd@}\) [[if test="is(w=10)"]]minutes[[else]]km[[/if]], the standard deviation in the units of the data.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
