  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Statistics II: standard deviation of grouped data</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core and Essential 3.1: Use class midpoints to estimate the mean and standard deviation of grouped data.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question D3 in Section D of Chapter 2 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P. and Shilton, S., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Statistics 1 for Edexcel, Cambridge University Press, 2004: extended from the mean to the standard deviation and randomised, with new Kenyan contexts and new data.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
